    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d452">

                <pb facs="0686" n="584" xml:id="pg584"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">883.101/11</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in Egypt</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Childs</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 198</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-11-03">November 3,
                        1936</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Reference is made to the Legation’s
                    despatch No. 710 of July 6, 1936,<anchor n="26" xml:id="d452-f1"/> requesting
                    instructions as to the attitude to be adopted by the Consul General at
                    Alexandria in connection with certain proposals presented by the British Consul
                    General concerning the election of foreign members of the Municipal Council of
                    Alexandria.</p>
                <p>In view of the probable early termination of the Capitulations in Egypt, the
                    Department is of the opinion that it would be inadvisable for the Consul General
                    to discuss at this time any proposals for the appointment or election of members
                    of the Municipal Council of Alexandria, particularly since the question of
                    American representation on the Council during the active regime of the
                    Capitulations is of restricted interest to this Government.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>R. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Walton Moore</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
